course: dictionary
lesson: 8375
title: Rover: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and rover is a good example. Read the words around it to find out which meaning the writer means. «A Mars rover drives itself short distances.» Here a rover is a machine, because it drives and it is on Mars.
explain: Other clues point to other meanings. In a story, «Rover» with a capital letter may be a dog's name, and «a rover» may be a traveller who wanders from place to place. Check your choice by putting it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
explain: The dictionary lists the meanings as 1), 2), 3) and so on. Read them all, then choose the one that fits the sentence best. You do not have to pick the first one.
fact: A rover is a vehicle that drives across the surface of another planet or the Moon to explore it.
fact: Mars rovers such as Curiosity and Perseverance take photos, drill rocks and look for signs of water and past life.
fact: Rovers are robots controlled from Earth, and radio signals take minutes to travel between Mars and Earth, so a rover drives itself short distances.
fact: Rover is also an old-fashioned common name for a pet dog, and a rover can be a person who wanders from place to place.
fact: Scientists test Mars rovers in the Atacama Desert in Chile, because its dry, lifeless soil is a little like Mars.
exercise: «The rover Perseverance carried a small helicopter called Ingenuity.» In this sentence, what is a rover? | A kind of desert | A traveller with no home | A pet dog | *A robot vehicle that explores another planet
exercise: «In the story, Rover wagged his tail and barked at the postman.» What is Rover in this story? | A Rover Scout leader | A Mars rover | *A pet dog | A storm on Mars
exercise: «The rover wandered from town to town, with no home and no job.» What does rover mean here? | A helicopter | A robot on the Moon | *A traveller who wanders from place to place | A type of desert
test: «A storm in 2018 covered the solar panels of the rover Opportunity, and it never woke again.» What is the rover Opportunity? | A helicopter that flew on Mars | A dog that never woke up | A dust storm | *A robot vehicle that explored Mars
test: Jay says rover always means a pet dog. Why is he wrong? | Rover is only used in stories, never in science | *A pet dog is only one meaning, and the context shows which meaning fits | Rover always means a desert | Rover means a helicopter
exam: Which meaning of rover fits «The lunar rover took photos of the grey plains on the Moon»? | A pet dog | *A vehicle that drives around a planet or Moon to explore it | A Rover Scout | A traveller with no home
